# XCU return
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The special built-in utilities are described inside
# utilities/V3_chap02.html (the page utilities/return.html only redirects
# there), so anchors name V3_chap02.html and the .cov file accounts for
# the units by hand.

assertion  XCU.return.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/stop executing the current function
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/The exit status shall be <i>n</i>
class      required
says       return n ends the function with status n and the rest of the
           function is not run.
test       t/001-function-status.sh

assertion  XCU.return.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/the result shall be as if <i>n</i> were specified
class      required
says       return with no operand uses the status of the last command
           executed.
test       t/002-no-operand.sh

assertion  XCU.return.003
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.5
class      required
says       After return, execution resumes with the command after the
           function call.
test       t/003-resume.sh

assertion  XCU.return.004
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/dot script
class      required
says       return in a file read by the dot utility stops that file; the
           shell continues after the dot command with the status given.
test       t/004-dot-script.sh

assertion  XCU.return.005
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/stop executing the current function
class      required
says       return inside loops, if and case commands of a function ends the
           function at once.
test       t/005-nested-compound.sh

assertion  XCU.return.006
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/stop executing the current function
class      required
says       return ends only the function it is in; a calling function
           carries on.
test       t/006-innermost-function.sh
